# Harvest v3 (OAuth 2.0 client credentials) — Configure > Dev Center > API Credentials >
# Create new API credentials > "Harvest V3 (OAuth)". Grant the scopes for the tools you use.
# The client secret is shown once — store it immediately.
GREENHOUSE_CLIENT_ID=your-harvest-v3-client-id
GREENHOUSE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-harvest-v3-client-secret

# Optional: public job board tools (your board URL slug). Enough on its own for board-only mode.
# GREENHOUSE_BOARD_TOKEN=your-board-url-slug
# Optional: Job Board API key, only needed to submit applications through the board API
# GREENHOUSE_BOARD_API_KEY=your-job-board-api-key

# Optional: Greenhouse user ID (numeric, from the user's URL in Greenhouse).
# When set:
#   - write operations are made as this user (the OAuth token's `sub`), for the audit trail
#   - the server reads the user's role at startup and derives the tool profile:
#       site_admin=true → full profile (all tools, all jobs)
#       has job permissions → recruiter profile (writes scoped to permitted jobs only)
#       no permissions → read-only profile
#       deactivated user → server refuses to start
# Reads always use the credential's integration service user, because v3 list endpoints
# require Site Admin authorization.
# GREENHOUSE_USER_ID=your-greenhouse-user-id

# Optional: tool profile — full (default), recruiter, or read-only
# Ignored when GREENHOUSE_USER_ID is set (profile is derived automatically).
# GREENHOUSE_TOOL_PROFILE=recruiter

# Optional: shorthand for GREENHOUSE_TOOL_PROFILE=read-only
# GREENHOUSE_READ_ONLY=true

# Optional: Ingestion API (partner candidate submission) — Basic-auth key for that API
# GREENHOUSE_INGESTION_API_KEY=your-ingestion-api-key

# Optional: structured JSON logging (debug, info, warning, error)
# GREENHOUSE_LOG_LEVEL=info
# GREENHOUSE_LOG_FILE=/var/log/greenhouse-mcp.log

# Optional: webhook receiver settings
# GREENHOUSE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your-webhook-secret-key
# WEBHOOK_DB_PATH=~/.open-greenhouse-mcp/webhooks.db
# PORT=8080
